  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This review synthesized 99 studies on digital twins (DTs) for intelligent intersections across five core themes: software architectures, data pipelines, AI-driven traffic control, vulnerable road user safety, and network scaling. By evaluating systems against explicit levels of operational coupling, it mapped current progress in edge-to-cloud deployments, co-simulation, and reinforcement learning while framing open challenges in real-world validation, interoperability, and governance.",
      "why": "It establishes clear taxonomies that separate true bidirectional digital twins from simpler digital shadows or isolated simulators, preventing conceptual confusion as cities evaluate real-time traffic monitoring systems."
    }
  },
